{title: I Lift My Eyes to the Mountains}
{subtitle: Psalm 121}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 79}
{time: 6/8}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [Eb] | [Eb] |
| [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
I lift my eyes to the mountains
[Ab]Where will my [Bb]help come [Eb]from?
My help comes from the [Ab]LORD
Who made [Eb]heav[Bb]en and [Cm]earth
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Eb]My help comes from the [Ab]LORD
Who made [Eb]heav[Bb]en and [Eb]earth
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
He will not let your foot slip
He who [Ab]watches over [Bb]you will not [Eb]slumber
See, he [Ebmaj7/G]who watches o[Ab]ver Israel
[Eb]Will neither [Bb]slumber nor [Cm]sleep
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
The [Cm]LORD watches [Ab]over [Eb]you
The [Cm]LORD is your shade at your [Ab]right [Eb]side
The [Cm]sun will not strike you by [Ab]day
Nor the [Eb]moon [Bb]by [Cm]night
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Eb] | [Eb] |
| [Cm] | [Ab] [Eb] | ×4

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Eb]The LORD will keep you from all harm
He will watch over your life
The LORD will watch over your going out and your [Bb]coming [Cm7]in
[Eb]Now and fo[Bb]rever[Eb]more
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
My help comes from the [Ab]LORD
Who made [Eb]heav[Bb]en and [Eb]earth
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Your [Cm]going out and your [Ab]coming [Eb]in
Now and fo[Bb]rever[Eb]more
{end_of_verse}
